-- title:
--   Diamond operators with d ≡ 1 (mod M) fix each finite-chart component
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), namely the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\mathrm{Frac}(A) = L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$, and let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), with $j \neq 0$. Let $d$ be coprime to $Mp$ with $d \equiv 1 \pmod M$, and let $\theta$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ which, under the identification $hK$ (i.e. on elements with equal Laurent expansions), has the same Laurent expansions as the base change to $L$, via [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24), of [`ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L66). Let $\rho$ be a ring endomorphism of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$, whose values in $K$ agree with $\theta$. Then every minimal prime $\mathfrak{P}$ over the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in that chart algebra satisfies $\rho^{-1}(\mathfrak{P}) = \mathfrak{P}$.
--
--   In terms of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$, this says that the automorphism of the special fibre induced by the diamond operator $\langle d \rangle$ with $d \equiv 1 \pmod M$ maps each irreducible component meeting the $j$-finite chart into itself; the number of such components is not part of the assertion. It feeds into the construction of the induced automorphism of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ compatible with the crossings of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_comap_eq_self_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_apply_eq_diamondAut_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul.lean

